---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const seoTitle = "Terms & Conditions & Good Faith Estimate | Odyssey Insights";
const seoDescription = "Website terms of use and No Surprises Act Good Faith Estimate notice for Odyssey Insights Counseling LLC in St. Cloud, Minnesota.";
---

<Layout title={seoTitle} description={seoDescription}>
  <Header />
  
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-6 text-slate-700">
      
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-6 mb-8 text-center">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Website Terms & Conditions of Use</h1>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Last Updated: October 19, 2026</p>
        <p class="text-sm">Owner: Odyssey Insights Counseling LLC (Brian Oduguwa, MSW, LICSW)</p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Please read these Terms & Conditions carefully before using <a href="https://www.odysseyinsightscounseling.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">www.odysseyinsightscounseling.com</a>. By accessing or using this website, you agree to the terms below.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-2">1. Informational & Educational Purpose Only (No Clinical Advice)</h2>
      <p>
        All content on this website—including text describing couples therapy, the Gottman Method, Emotionally Focused Therapy (EFT), EMDR, Cognitive Processing Therapy (CPT), blog posts, FAQs, and resource links—is provided strictly for general informational and educational purposes. Nothing on this website constitutes individualized psychotherapy, medical advice, psychiatric diagnosis, or clinical treatment.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-2">2. No Therapist-Client Relationship Created by Website Use</h2>
      <p>
        Viewing this website, downloading resources, calling our office number, sending an email, or submitting a website contact form does not create a therapist-client relationship with Brian Oduguwa, MSW, LICSW or Odyssey Insights Counseling LLC. A formal clinical relationship is established only after:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2">
        <li>We have completed an initial screening or consultation to confirm clinical fit and licensure jurisdiction;</li>
        <li>You have reviewed and electronically signed the formal Informed Consent for Psychotherapy, Practice Policies, and HIPAA/Minnesota Health Records Act Privacy agreements inside our secure client portal; and</li>
        <li>Your first clinical intake appointment has commenced.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-2">3. Not a Crisis or Emergency Service</h2>
      <p>
        Odyssey Insights Counseling LLC is an outpatient, appointment-based private practice and does not provide 24/7 crisis response or emergency mental health intervention. Electronic messages and voicemail are not monitored continuously. If you are experiencing a medical or psychiatric emergency, thoughts of suicide, or domestic violence, call <strong>911</strong>, call or text <strong>988</strong> (Suicide & Crisis Lifeline), or contact the Central Minnesota 24/7 Mental Health Crisis Line at <strong>(320) 253-5555</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-2">4. Licensure Jurisdiction & Telehealth Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        Brian Oduguwa, MSW, LICSW is licensed by the Minnesota Board of Social Work (LICSW License #22350). Clinical psychotherapy services are offered only to individuals and couples who are physically located within the State of Minnesota (or another jurisdiction where the provider holds active licensure or regulatory authorization) at the time of each session, in accordance with Minnesota Statutes Chapter 148E and the Minnesota Telehealth Act (Minn. Stat. § 62A.673).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-2">5. Fees, Good Faith Estimate & Cancellation Policy</h2>
      <p>
        Standard private-pay fees ($150 per 60-minute individual session; $180 per 90-minute couples session) are published transparently on our <a href="/services" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Scheduling & Services pages</a>. In accordance with the federal No Surprises Act (45 CFR § 149.610), all self-pay and out-of-network clients are entitled to receive a written Good Faith Estimate of expected charges upon scheduling or request. Appointment cancellations require at least 24 hours' advance notice as detailed in the signed Client Intake Agreement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-2">6. Intellectual Property & Copyright</h2>
      <p>
        All original text, branding, layout design, and clinical descriptions on this website are the intellectual property of Odyssey Insights Counseling LLC and may not be copied, scraped for commercial republication, or reproduced without written permission. Literary epigraphs cited on this website (Kino no Tabi) remain the property of their respective authors and are quoted under fair use.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-2">7. Governing Law & Venue</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms & Conditions and any dispute arising from your use of this website shall be governed by the laws of the State of Minnesota, with exclusive venue in Stearns County, Minnesota.
      </p>

    </article>
  </main>
  
  <Footer />
</Layout>